From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Settings > Apps > Default apps

ChromeOS sets the app a kind of file opens with only from Files' "Open
with" menu ("Change default"). NickelOS adds a Default apps card to the
Apps page: for images, videos, music, PDF documents and text files, the
apps that can open them (ChromeOS's own, web apps, Linux apps) and the one
they open with. Choosing one writes the defaults Files keeps, for all the
kind's types and extensions. Linux apps open files through ChromeOS
(nickel-open, Chrome 0020), so the same defaults apply to them.

NickelDefaultAppsHandler finds the apps the way Files does (file_tasks,
for a sample file of each kind in Downloads) and sets the default with
UpdateDefaultTask; the card is the nickel-default-apps element.

